<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russian conquest of Central Asia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1839">1839</a>–<a href="/years/1895">1895</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russian conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> was the gradual annexation of the Kazakh steppe and the khanates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> in the nineteenth century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> fell in 1865 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> in 1868, Khiva was subdued in 1873 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> were defeated at Geok Tepe in 1881. The region became Russian Turkestan, with Bukhara and Khiva left as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorates</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russian-conquest-of-central-asia.jpg" alt="Russian conquest of Central Asia" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nikolay Karazin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9D%D0%B0%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%B3_%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B0%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B2_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B5_%D1%82%D1%83%D0%B7%D0%B5%D0%BC%D1%86%D0%B5%D0%B2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
